# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DORIS autopilot configuration for SITL.
#
# Layered ON TOP of ArduSub's Tools/autotest/default_params/sub.parm
# (see launch_sitl.sh / entrypoint_ardusub.sh --defaults ordering).
#
# This file only carries:
#   1. What must be true BEFORE doris.lua runs (e.g. scripting enabled).
#   2. Hardware wiring the script depends on (relay + light servo).
#
# It deliberately does NOT duplicate the many params doris.lua re-asserts
# itself at boot via set_and_save() — ARMING_CHECK, FS_*, EK3_SRC1_*,
# SERVO13_FUNCTION, BARO_SPEC_GRAV, BATT_FS_*, DISARM_DELAY — so there is
# a single source of truth for those (the Lua).  The one exception is
# SERVO13_FUNCTION below, pre-seeded so the light mapping is correct on
# the very first cycle.
#
# ⚠ CONFIRM the lines marked "CONFIRM" against a real-vehicle parameter
#   dump before trusting SITL results for relay / battery behavior.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# --- Lua scripting -----------------------------------------------------------
# Must be enabled before the autopilot will load scripts/doris.lua.
SCR_ENABLE       1
# doris.lua is large (38-entry param table, ring buffers, lots of string
# formatting). Give the Lua VM generous heap so allocation never fails.
SCR_HEAP_SIZE    200000

# --- Drop-weight relay -------------------------------------------------------
# doris.lua drives relay instance DORIS_RELAY_CH (default 0 -> RELAY1) via
# relay:on()/relay:off(). The relay must be assigned to a GPIO pin and have
# a Relay function for the binding to actuate hardware.
# Per "Doris Setup instructions": Relay function 1, Relay 1 pin 14.
RELAY1_FUNCTION  1     # CONFIRM: 1 = Relay
RELAY1_PIN       14    # CONFIRM: BCM/AUX pin driving the burn-wire relay

# --- Lights ------------------------------------------------------------------
# SERVO13 -> RCIN9 (59). doris.lua also sets this at boot; pre-seeding keeps
# the mapping correct on the first update cycle before the Lua runs.
SERVO13_FUNCTION 59

# --- Battery monitor ---------------------------------------------------------
# Analog voltage+current so battery:voltage(0) / capacity_remaining_pct(0)
# return real values for the pre-arm and low-battery failsafe checks.
BATT_MONITOR     4     # CONFIRM: monitor type / analog pin mapping
